        "title": "feat(ui): add mobile Red voice surface",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Adds a dedicated mobile-first `/voice?session=main` Control UI route for Red voice sessions.\n- Reuses existing Gateway auth and browser-owned `talk.client.create` WebRTC flow.\n- Adds navigation, responsive styling, tests, and i18n keys for the new voice surface.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\nThe existing Talk controls lived inside the full chat composer, which is workable on desktop but awkward on mobile. This PR gives browser/mobile users a focused voice-first surface while preserving the current Gateway auth boundary, browser-owned WebRTC setup, and Red agent-consult routing.\n\n## Evidence\n- `pnpm ui:i18n:check` passed after rebasing on current upstream `main`.\n- `pnpm --dir ui exec vitest run --project unit src/ui/views/voice.test.ts src/ui/navigation.test.ts` passed: 2 files, 30 tests.\n- `pnpm --dir ui exec vitest run --project chromium src/ui/navigation.browser.test.ts` passed: 1 file, 17 tests.\n- `pnpm ui:build` passed.\n- Before PR creation, `pnpm test:ui` passed locally: 153 files, 2528 tests.\n- Live Gateway readback showed loopback `127.0.0.1:18789`; local `/voice?session=main` returned HTTP 200.\n- In-app mobile viewport render check showed `Start Talk`, `Ready`, `Open chat`, no horizontal overflow.\n- Microphone start was intentionally not exercised by automation because it requires the user browser permission prompt.",
